pmc:NippurText3HouseholdKeptFromTheDestroyer a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A household kept from the destroyer who parts husband from wife"@en, "Ein Hausstand bewahrt vor dem Verderber, der Mann von Frau trennt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The bowl is designated a spell and mystery and strong seal for the sealing of a named household, that the evil demon and the evil satan called the Mighty Destroyer depart and remove: that he not kill off the man from his wife nor the wife from her husband nor their sons and daughters, whether those they have or those they shall have, from this day and forever, neither by night nor by day."@en ;
    skos:note "The operative part is a chain of mystical syllables called the great name, before which the angel of death is afraid and from which, hearing it, he flees frightened and is swallowed up; the same clause is set out four times over in the one text, each time ending in the same word of sealing. The claim covers children not yet born, which is the ordinary reach of these charms and is stated in every bowl that mentions offspring."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 3: 1-11, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 127-128)" .

