pmc:NippurText5ManAndSistersKeptFromTheEvilEye a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A man and his two sisters kept from the evil eye and the mighty satan"@en, "Ein Mann und seine zwei Schwestern bewahrt vor dem bösen Blick und dem mächtigen Satan"@de ;
    skos:definition "All evil liliths and all demons and devils and spells and idol-spirits, and the Vow and the Curse and the Invocation, and evil arts and mighty works and everything hostile are to depart from a named man and his two sisters. They are bound with the seven spells and sealed with the seven seals, and the great Prince is conjured to keep the man and one sister from the Evil Eye and from the mighty Satan and from the many Satyrs in the road of Hamad."@en ;
    skos:note "A named road, which is the only topographical specification in the collection, and a named class of spirit attached to it. The bowl closes with two scriptural passages in Hebrew, the march at the mouth of Yhwh and the rebuke of Satan, the second of which recurs in three other bowls of this collection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 5: 1-6, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 138-139)" .

