pmc:NippurText6DemonsPressedDownFromACouple a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "The demons of a couple pressed down, blind to them in dream and sleep"@en, "Die Dämonen eines Paares niedergepresst, blind für sie in Traum und Schlaf"@de ;
    skos:definition "A press which is pressed down upon the demons, devils, satans, amulet-spirits, familiars, counter-charms and liliths male and female that attach themselves to a named couple, dwell in their archways, lurk by their thresholds, appear to them in one form and another, and strike and cast down and kill. The stated outcome: that they appear to the couple neither in dream by night nor in sleep by day, that they approach neither their right side nor their left, that they kill not their children, and that they have no power over their property, what they have and what they shall have, from this day and forever."@en ;
    skos:note "The bowl that names the vessel a press and uses the verb of pressing of its own operation four times. The pressing is done by seven words, each attached to a named power, by which heaven and earth are charmed; the seventh of those names is itself the word for presses."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 6: 1-11, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 141-142)" .

