pmc:NippurText7LifeHouseAndBodyBoundAndSealed a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "The life, house, property and bedchamber of a man bound and sealed"@en, "Leben, Haus, Habe und Schlafkammer eines Mannes gebunden und gesiegelt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The bowl binds, seals and counterseals the life, house and property of a named man in the name of the great God and with the seal of Shadda El, by the splendour of Sebaoth and by the great glory of the Holy One, that all demons and all mighty satans remove and betake themselves and go out from the house and from the dwelling and from the whole body of the man; and then binds, seals and counterseals the same again, together with his bedchamber, in the name of Gabriel and Michael and Raphael, of the angel Asiel and Ermes the great Lord, of the great Abbahu and of the great Abraxas, the guardian of good spirits and destroyer of evil."@en ;
    skos:note "The best preserved text of the collection is a replica of this one published two years earlier from another bowl of the same museum, and the editor prints the two in parallel columns throughout. The clients of this bowl are the operators of text 27, where the man works the charm in his own name instead of receiving it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 7: 1-9, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 147-148)" .

