pmc:NippurText9DivorcesWrittenForAllTheLiliths a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "Divorces written for all the liliths that appear to a man and his wife"@en, "Scheidebriefe für alle Lilithen, die einem Mann und seiner Frau erscheinen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The operator deposits and sinks the bowl, operates the work in the fashion of Rabbi Joshua bar Perahia, and writes divorces for all the liliths who appear to a named couple in dream by night and in slumber by day: a writ of separation and divorce, by virtue of letter abstracted from letter and letters from letters, of word from words and of pronunciation from pronunciations, whereby heaven and earth are swallowed up, the mountains are uprooted and the heights melt away. He has mounted up over them to the celestial height and brought a destroyer against them, to bring them forth from the house and dwelling and threshold and bedchamber."@en ;
    skos:note "The one bowl that describes its own deposition in the first person at the head of the text, which is how the position of the excavated vessels and the wording of the corpus were brought together. The letter-from-letter clause is the corpus at its most explicit about where it locates the power: in the manipulation of the written sign and the pronunciation, not in the being invoked."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 9: 1-11, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 161-162)" .

