pmc:NippurText10HouseholdSealedWithTheSealsOfAdamAndNoah a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A household sealed with the seals of the First Adam and of Noah"@en, "Ein Hausstand gesiegelt mit den Siegeln des ersten Adam und Noahs"@de ;
    skos:definition "An amulet for the salvation of a named woman, her husband, her son, her house and her whole threshold. The house and threshold are sealed and countersealed; the woman and her son are sealed with that seal with which the First Adam sealed Seth his son and he was preserved from demons and devils and tormentors and satans; and the three of them are sealed and countersealed again with that seal with which Noah sealed the ark from the waters of the Deluge, that the spirits may fly and cease and go forth and remove from them and from their house and their abode and their bed-chamber, from this day and forever."@en ;
    skos:note "Both warrants are sealings that are said to have worked once before, and both name what they preserved against. The editor notes that this is one of the two bowls in which the father of the client is named instead of the mother, and that here the woman’s husband and father bore the same name."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 10: 1-6, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 165)" .

