pmc:NippurText11WomanSavedFromFeverBarrennessAndAbortion a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A woman saved from the lilith, fever, barrenness and abortion"@en, "Eine Frau gerettet vor der Lilith, Fieber, Unfruchtbarkeit und Fehlgeburt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salvation from heaven for a named woman, that she be saved by the love of heaven from the Lilith and the Tormentor; that these and Fever and Barrenness and Abortion fly and refrain and remove from her, in the name of him who controls the demons and devils and liliths. The bowl is for the binding of Bagdana, their king and ruler; it adjures the named lilith who dwells in her house and plagues boys and girls; it has written her a divorce and separated her as the demons do who write divorces for their wives and do not return to them; and it tells her to take her divorce, not to appear by night or by day, not to lie with the woman and not to kill her sons and daughters."@en ;
    skos:note "One of four nearly identical inscriptions, the others being text 18 of this collection, a Mandaic bowl published by another editor and the very first bowl of this class ever published; the editor restores the broken halves of each from the others. The four harms are named as four separate things, which is as near as this corpus comes to a list of complaints."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 11: 1-9, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 170)" .

