pmc:NippurText12OffspringAndPreservation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "Offspring, long standing and preservation for a family of nine"@en, "Nachkommen, Bestand und Bewahrung für eine Familie von neun"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salvation from heaven for a named man, his wife, their seven named children, their house and their property, that they may have offspring and may live and be established and be preserved from demons and devils and plagues and satans and curses and liliths and tormentors which may appear to them. The angel adjured, and compelled by the rubric inside the text, together with those like him, will frustrate and ban all familiars and countercharms and necklace-spirits and curses and invocations and knockings and rites and words and demons and devils and plagues and liliths and idol-spirits and tormentors and everything whatsoever evil, that they flee and depart from the household and its dwelling from this day and forever."@en ;
    skos:note "The same family stands in text 16 and in the two Syriac bowls 31 and 33, so four bowls of three dialects were made for one house. The exterior of this bowl carries an endorsement naming where it was to lie: of the inner room, of the hall."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 12: 1-12, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 174-175)" .

