pmc:NippurText14NamedAndUnnamedDemonsCastDown a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A woman sealed against demons whose names are written and whose are not"@en, "Eine Frau gesiegelt gegen Dämonen, deren Namen geschrieben sind und deren nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The bowl is made for the sealing of a named woman. It adjures the evil one in the name of holy Agrabis and of further names, and him who lodged his Shekina in the temple of light and hail; it invokes Michael and Gabriel, Sariel, Seraphiel, Suriel, Sarsamiel, Gadriel, Peniel and Nahriel; and it binds all blast-demons and evil injurers, whose names are recorded in this bowl and whose names are not recorded in this bowl, to be cast down and to sit within the glowing light and fiery flame."@en ;
    skos:note "The clause covering the unrecorded names is the craft’s own provision against the insufficiency of its instrument, and it is this bowl that states it most plainly. The editor reads several of the opening names as letter-substitutions and anagrams for the divine name rather than as beings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 14: 1-8, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 183)" .

