    pm:byPractice pmp:NippurBowlInversion ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:NippurText14NamedAndUnnamedDemonsCastDown ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 14: 1-8, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 183)" .

pmc:NippurText15HouseholdBoundWithBrassIronAndFire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A household banished of its spirits by a rhyming couplet and a seal of fire"@en, "Ein Hausstand durch einen Reimspruch und ein Feuersiegel von seinen Geistern befreit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salvation of heaven for the house and dwelling of five named persons. The operative part is a doggerel couplet printed in Latin letters, repeated three times with variation, after which the operator says: I scan and rhyme against you, Spirits and Goblins and Plagues and Howlers and Strokes and Circlet-spirits and evil arts and mighty works and idol-spirits and the evil Lilith; and I bind you with bonds of brass and iron and seal you with the figure of a seal of fire; and I banish you from the five, in the name of eight named angels, and by the seal of Yhwh Sebaoth it is established forever."@en ;
    skos:note "The editor says the virtue of this charm lies in the couplet, which is the only place in the collection where the working words are a measured verse rather than a list of names or a formula of binding. The figure in the centre of the bowl is the serpent with its tail in its mouth. The five clients may be the members of a lodging house."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 15: 1-9, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 185-186)" .

