pmc:NippurText16ChildrenLongLifeAndNoInjurerTouching a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "Children, long life and no injurer in the world touching a large family"@en, "Kinder, langes Leben und kein Schädiger der Welt, der eine große Familie berührt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salvation from heaven for the same family of nine, their house and their property, that they may have children and may live long and be established, and that no injurer in the world may touch them. It works by the great name whereby the holy God is called, which suppresses darkness under light, plague under healing, destruction under construction, injury under ban and anger under repose; by it all the sons of darkness are suppressed under the throne of God, and a list of twenty-odd kinds of hostile power, ending with the seven tormentors of night and day, are bound, suppressed and laid away from the family, their house, their property and all their abode, from this day forever."@en ;
    skos:note "The five pairs of the great name are the only statement in this corpus of how the binding is supposed to work rather than of what it binds, and each pair sets a good over an evil in the same construction. The list of species that follows is the longest in the collection."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 16: 1-14, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 188-189)" .

