pmc:NippurText18PrayerForOffspring a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "Offspring prayed for in the fourth of the duplicate divorce bowls"@en, "Nachkommenschaft, erbeten in der vierten der gleichlautenden Scheidungsschalen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fourth of the nearly identical inscriptions collated under text 11. The editor gives no translation, saying the bowl is badly written and mutilated and would be in large part unintelligible without the other texts, and that it presents little that is new; of its second line he states that a prayer for offspring is here expressed."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered because the bowl carries a statement of effect even though the volume prints no translation of it, and because leaving it out would make the count of the collection’s claims depend on how much of each bowl the editor chose to render. What the node rests on is one sentence of the commentary and not a read passage of the text; that is said here and not smoothed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 18: 2, with the commentary, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 193)" .

