pmc:NippurText20GhostsExorcisedFromAWoman a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "The demon, devil, satan, curse-spirit and liliths exorcised from a woman"@en, "Dämon, Teufel, Satan, Fluchgeist und Lilithen von einer Frau gebannt"@de ;
    skos:definition "In the name of a sixfold repeated letter, the Demon and the Devil and the Satan and the Curse-spirit and the evil Liliths which appear by night and appear by day, and appear to a named woman, are exorcised and sealed, in the name of Gabriel, Michael and Rophiel."@en ;
    skos:note "The shortest text of the collection and the one whose figure carries the claim: a demon drawn with arms and legs manacled, with the word prohibition written in the space at its right and permission at its left, and the client’s name inscribed in the lower part of the body on the side of the prohibition. The editor reads the picture as presenting graphically that the demon has no power over the lady, and calls the inscription itself very illiterate."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 20: 1-5, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 201)" .

