pmc:NippurText22HouseAndThresholdSealedSecondOfFour a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "House and threshold sealed from every kind of lilith, the second of a set"@en, "Haus und Schwelle gesiegelt vor jeder Art Lilith, die zweite eines Satzes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second and longest of the three surviving bowls of the set, and the one the volume translates. Sealed and countersealed are the house and threshold of the same woman from all evil plagues, from all evil spirits, and from the tormentors, and from the liliths, and from all injurers, that ye approach not to her, to the house and threshold, which is sealed with three signets and countersealed with seven seals from every kind of lilith and from all injurers, that ye approach not to her, and from all evil spirits and from all evil injurers, from this day and forever."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 22: 1-5, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 203-204)" .

