pmc:NippurText23HouseAndThresholdSealedThirdOfFour a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "House and threshold sealed from every kind of lilith, the third of a set"@en, "Haus und Schwelle gesiegelt vor jeder Art Lilith, die dritte eines Satzes"@de ;
    skos:definition "The third of the three surviving bowls of the set, carrying the same sealing of the house and threshold of the same woman against the same list of powers, with slight variations of wording. All three are roughly and illegibly written, and in all three a grammatical peculiarity recurs which the editor finds again in the Mandaic bowls."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 23: 1-4, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, pp. 203-204)" .

