pmc:NippurText24FirstSisterSavedFromFeverAndSweating a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "One sister saved from fever and from sweating"@en, "Eine Schwester gerettet vor Fieber und Schweißkrankheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first of three statements of effect on one bowl, each for a different daughter of one woman and each naming its own malady: salvation from heaven be for the first, that she be saved by the love of heaven from Fever and from Sweating."@en ;
    skos:note "This bowl is counted as three claims and not one, because it states three different outcomes for three named persons in three separate formulas each closed with its own Amen. The editor calls it a charm for three daughters made out in their names severally and for specific maladies. The names of the two diseases are broken at the third term."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 24: 1-3, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 205)" .

