pmc:NippurText24SecondSisterFreedOfDisturbingDreams a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A second sister freed of disturbing dreams and the evil spirit"@en, "Eine zweite Schwester befreit von störenden Träumen und dem bösen Geist"@de ;
    skos:definition "The second statement of effect on the same bowl: salvation from heaven be for the second daughter, that there cease from her disturbing dreams and the evil spirit and evil satans."@en ;
    skos:note "The disturbing dream is the one complaint in this corpus that is both the harm and the observable: elsewhere the charms forbid the demon to appear in dream by night, and here the dream itself is what the bowl is to stop."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 24: 3-4, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 205)" .

