pmc:NippurText25FamilyGhostsKeptFromTheLiving a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:AramaicIncantationTextsFromNippur ;
    rdfs:label "A couple kept from the apparition of their own dead"@en, "Ein Paar bewahrt vor der Erscheinung seiner eigenen Toten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Salvation from heaven for a named man and his wife, that there vanish from them in their dwelling the demons and devils by the mercy of heaven. Then the clause the bowl exists for: whoever here has dead, who shall become alive to them here, and shall approach and are found to be actually dead, from these you are kept and these are kept from you. A message is to be sent to a named one of the departed about the contentions of them all; and five named angels, who bring salvation to all the children of men, will come and go forth with the salvation of the house and property and dwelling and the sons and daughters and all the people in the house, from this day even for the sphere of eternity."@en ;
    skos:note "The one bowl of the collection directed against the apparition of a household’s own dead rather than against a class of spirit, and the only one that proposes to negotiate: the dead are to be told to cease their contentions with the living. The editor compares two bowls of other collections and notes that the name given to the departed is a fancy name and not recognisable as a person’s."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:JewishPracticalMagic ;
    dcterms:source "Aramaic Incantation Texts from Nippur, text 25: 1-7, ed. and trans. J. A. Montgomery (Publications of the Babylonian Section III, Philadelphia 1913, p. 207)" .

